AI for Real-Time Strategy and Adaptive Gameplay
Real-time strategy games are a very good example for such applications, where AI systems, such as PINSKY, and the Poet Algorithm, are used to make decisions and optimize strategies as well as build intuition regarding different situations.[11]
This way the technique let us make dynamic game reactions in a game to tactics of the player, that is raise its difficulty and interest. 
For instance: -
StarCraft: Based on reinforcement learning, EISBot’s Brood War allows the maximisation of decisions based on real time actions being made by a player to optimise unit control.[10]
Relic Entertainment used AI to give the challenge level a dynamic change in the Age of Empires IV game just to keep it exciting for all skill levels players.

AI and Technostress
The use of AI in automation of repetitive tasks reduces technostress among game developers. AI can automate most tasks for example, generating textures, management of enemy waves or crafting quests, so the AI frees up game designers time to focus more on creative roles which reduces burnout and improves job satisfaction.[6]

